== Cooking rice ==

Rinse @basmati rice{1%cup}(preferably aged) very well in water till the starch clears from the water. The water should be clear and not cloudy or opaque.

Then soak the rice in water for ~{30%minutes}. Later drain the rice well and keep aside.

Bring @water{4%cups} to a rolling boil in a #pot.

Add whole spices - @cinnamon{1%inch}, @tej patta{1}(medium-sized or 2 small), @cloves{2 - 3}, @green cardamoms{2 - 3}, @shahi jeera{1/4%teaspoon}(caraway seeds). Also add @salt{1%teaspoon}.

Now add the soaked rice. Do not stir the rice.

Keep the flame to high and cook the rice without lowering the temperature.

The rice grains have to be cooked till 75% or ¾ done. They should have a bite to them when eaten.

Drain the rice in a #colander. You can also rinse the rice grains to remove starch if any and to stop the grains from cooking. Cover with a #lid and keep the rice aside.

== Making birista or fried onions ==

When the rice is soaking, prep the ingredients for the biryani. Slice the @onions{1%cup}(thinly sliced). Heat the @oil{4%tablespoons}(or ghee) in a small #frying pan and add the sliced onions.

Stir and begin to fry the onions till they turn golden. Add one or two pinches of @salt{pinch} for quick browning of the onions. Stir often for uniform browning and fry on a low flame.

Here the onions have begun to get golden.

Once the onions become golden, then remove them with a #slotted spoon and place them on #kitchen paper towels{}. Keep the fried onions aside.

== Preparation for marination ==

Warm the @milk{1/4%cup} on stove top or in the microwave. Add @saffron strands{16 to 18} to the milk. Stir and keep aside.

Whisk @Curd{1/2%cup}(full fat yogurt, fresh) in a #mixing bowl until smooth.

Add @ginger paste{1%teaspoon}(or 1 inch ginger crushed), @garlic paste{1%teaspoon}(or 4 to 5 cloves crushed), @green chilies{1%teaspoon}(chopped), @coriander leaves{1%tablespoon}(chopped) and @mint leaves{1/2%tablespoon}(chopped). Mix well.

Now add the spices - @turmeric powder{1/4%teaspoon}, @Red Chili Powder{1/4%teaspoon}(or cayenne pepper), @Garam Masala{1/4%teaspoon}, @Coriander Powder{1/2%teaspoon}, @shahi jeera{1/4%teaspoon}(caraway seeds) and @lemon juice{1%teaspoon}.

And @salt{as required}. Mix again.

Then add the half of the fried onions and the @Paneer{200 to 250%grams}(cubed).

Mix gently. Cover and keep the marinated paneer aside for ~{30%minutes}.

== Assembling and layering ==

Add the same oil in which we fried the onions to a #pan or #pot.

Add the marinated paneer and layer neatly.

Make a rice layer now. Add all the rice. I have just made two layers. If you want you can make four layers.

Add the remaining fried onions, @coriander leaves{1%tablespoon}(chopped) and @mint leaves{1/2%tablespoon}(chopped).

Sprinkle the saffron infused milk.

Dot with @Ghee{1 to 2%tablespoons}. You can also add @?rose water{1%tablespoon}(or kewra water).

== Dum cooking paneer biryani ==

Cover with a #aluminium foil or with a moist #kitchen cotton towel{}.

Place the #lid tightly on the pan and place it on a #tava or #griddle. For the first ~{5%minutes} dum cook the biryani on a medium heat.

Then lower the flame and cook the biryani.

On dum for ~{12-15%minutes}. You can also cook the biryani in a preheated #oven for ~{20-25%minutes} at 180 degrees C (350 degrees F). Use an oven proof pot or pan.

Serve the Paneer Biryani hot with boondi raita or cucumber raita or onion raita or kuchumber salad.

== Serving Suggestions ==

> Enjoy Paneer Biryani hot or warm with raita like an onion-tomato raita or cucumber raita or boondi raita. You can also serve with sliced onion-lime salad or onion-tomato-cucumber salad.

> Pairing it with curries like mirchi ka salan and bagara baingan also tastes awesome. Even a simple plain yogurt tastes nice with it.

== Storage ==

> Place any leftovers in any sealed box or container and refrigerate for 1 to 2 days. Reheat by warming in the oven at 90 degrees Celsius (190 degrees Fahrenheit) or by steaming in the Instant pot for 5 minutes.